<title>PORTUGAL: Trawler owners lift blockade of Lisbon port.</title>
<headline>Trawler owners lift blockade of Lisbon port.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese trawlers lifted a 12-hour blockade of the port of Lisbon, the country's largest, on Thursday after the government agreed to talks on a dispute over a partial weekend ban on fishing.</p>
<p>Government officals were due to meet representatives of the trawler owners on Friday morning.</p>
<p>The blockade mounted by dozens of vessels began on Thursday morning in protest at the decision to ban fishing outside a 12 mile (19 km) limit for a 24-hour period each weekend in what the government said was a measure aimed at conserving stocks.</p>
<p>The fleet owners said the move was discriminatory because trawlers from neighbouring Spain could continue to fish undisturbed.</p>
</text>
